<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bridei son of Maelchon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 584</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Bridei I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bridei son of Maelchon was a powerful king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> in the second half of the 6th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adomnan">Adomnán</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/life-of-columba">Life of Columba</a> describes the saint visiting him at his fortress near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-ness">River Ness</a> in the 560s. Irish annals record his victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaels">Gaels</a> of Dal Riata around 558 and his death around 584.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bridei-son-of-maelchon.jpg" alt="Bridei son of Maelchon" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Hole · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Columba_converting_the_Picts.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
